Commands:
  daemon     Daemon lifecycle
  status     Daemon, workers, STOP latch, recording, viewers
  stop-all   STOP: latch all writes (only a user can release)
  events     Bounded read of recent events (live ring)
  mark       Put a marker on the shared timeline
  ui         Open the Loom UI for the user (TTY only), or focus a panel
  help       Commands (use --json for the canonical machine help)
  version    Version
  doctor     Check paths, permissions, daemon and port
  skills     Distribute bundled Loom agent skills locally
  confirm    Confirm a write with a token (only when the user enabled confirmations) (not in M1)
  approvals  List / wait for approvals (only when the user enabled approvals) (not in M1)
  run        Run a Loom script (not in M1)
  record     Recording sessions and export (not in M1)
  policy     Show / diff / propose policy (not in M1)
  echo       Simulated loopback device (sample domain)
  uart       Serial consoles — the user sees the same bytes live in the Loom UI
  can        CAN / CAN FD through the Loom daemon (M1: sim bus); the user sees it live in the Loom UI
  uds        ECU diagnostics over UDS (DoIP; `--sim bench` = virtual ECU behind loopback DoIP)
  eth        Ethernet capture/decode (tshark-style): DoIP, UDS over DoIP, SOME/IP
  psu        Bench power supply (M1: SimPsu)
  test       TC sessions with evidence-backed verdicts

